From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] nx2: deleted buffers and images waiting for the GPU are destroyed early past a limit (waveydude's 0912 part, EDEN_NX2_BC_PENDING_MIB / EDEN_NX2_TC_PENDING_MIB / EDEN_NX2_BC_PENDING_LOG), off by default

What: a deleted buffer keeps its memory for 8 frames (delayed_destruction_ring), and every buffer
that grows leaves its old copy there; a deleted image waits until the GPU is past it, looked at
once a frame. At an area load frames take seconds, so all of that waits through the load, at the
moment memory is shortest. In waveydude's crash at a later area's gate (base PS5 13.60) GPU-only
buffers went from 219 MiB in 289 buffers to 1,464 MiB in 1,626 within 2 s and the pool refused
the area's images. In a hand-played T151 session the buffer cache went from 1 to 468 MiB at the first area load (250 s).

With EDEN_NX2_BC_PENDING_MIB=<MiB> (a number; unset or 0: off): when a draw or dispatch is about
to make a buffer (CreateBuffer, only while may_wait_for_memory: the buffer setup of a draw or
dispatch, both caches locked) and that many MiB of deleted buffers wait, the GPU is waited for and
they are destroyed (runtime.ReleaseForBuffer: the same call the refused-buffer path already makes
there, which also destroys the texture cache's deleted images the GPU is past).
EDEN_NX2_TC_PENDING_MIB=<MiB> does the same when that many MiB of deleted images wait
(TextureCache::SentencedBytes, read through a new hook of the Vulkan buffer cache runtime). Either
limit releases both. EDEN_NX2_BC_PENDING_LOG=1 (exact "1") only logs. Lines (stderr,
EDEN_BC_PENDING): what waits each time it passes its highest so far by 64 MiB, and the 1st, 2nd,
4th ... release.

Price: each release is a full GPU wait on the GPU thread (a hitch), at most once per buffer made
while over the limit; so set the limit high enough that it happens at loads only (his runs used
128-256 MiB).

New file video_core/buffer_cache/pending_destroy.h (his, unchanged): the ring's bytes, slot by
slot. Changed from his: comments; BC_PENDING_LOG is exact "1" (his: first character).

Off: one static check per buffer made (CreateBuffer), two adds per deleted buffer and a slot
reset per frame in the byte ring; one hook pointer. No wait, no line. Not in the kept-store stamp.

Origin and credit: waveydude, ocarina-private patch 0912 ("T120: integrate Build O and add idle
texture pressure cleanup"; the pending-release part is from his Build O), commits dc8796d and
3db885a.
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
index de7be13..8bcde22 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
@@ -165,6 +165,108 @@ void BufferCache<P>::CollectRefused() {
 template <class P>
 void BufferCache<P>::ReleaseFinished() {
     delayed_destruction_ring.Clear();
+    pending_destroy.Clear();
+}
+
+// EDEN_NX2_BC_PENDING_MIB=<MiB> (unset or 0: off, as before; waveydude's 0912): a deleted buffer
+// keeps its memory for TICKS_TO_DESTROY frames (delayed_destruction_ring), and every buffer that
+// grows leaves its old copy there. When a frame takes seconds (an area streaming in) everything
+// replaced during it waits. With the switch, a draw or dispatch about to make a buffer while that
+// many MiB wait first waits for the GPU and destroys them (the refused buffer's own relief,
+// runtime.ReleaseForBuffer, before a refusal instead of after one).
+// EDEN_NX2_TC_PENDING_MIB=<MiB> (unset or 0: off) does the same for deleted images, which wait for
+// the GPU to pass them but are only looked at once a frame. The wait and the destruction are the
+// same call, so either limit being reached releases both. Only where a refused buffer may already
+// wait (may_wait_for_memory: a draw's or dispatch's buffer setup, both caches locked).
+// EDEN_NX2_BC_PENDING_LOG=1 only logs (stderr, EDEN_BC_PENDING): a line each time what waits, or
+// what the buffers hold, passes its highest so far by 64 MiB. Either limit logs the same lines.
+template <class P>
+void BufferCache<P>::ReleasePendingBuffers() {
+    static const u64 limit = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_BC_PENDING_MIB");
+        const u64 mib = value != nullptr ? std::strtoull(value, nullptr, 10) : 0;
+        if (mib != 0) {
+            std::fprintf(stderr,
+                         "EDEN_BC_PENDING on: deleted buffers are destroyed early from %llu MiB "
+                         "waiting\n",
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(mib));
+        }
+        return mib << 20;
+    }();
+    static const u64 image_limit = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_TC_PENDING_MIB");
+        const u64 mib = value != nullptr ? std::strtoull(value, nullptr, 10) : 0;
+        if (mib != 0) {
+            std::fprintf(stderr,
+                         "EDEN_TC_PENDING on: deleted images are destroyed early from %llu MiB "
+                         "waiting\n",
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(mib));
+        }
+        return mib << 20;
+    }();
+    static const bool log = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_BC_PENDING_LOG");
+        return limit != 0 || image_limit != 0 ||
+               (value != nullptr && value[0] == '1' && value[1] == '\0');
+    }();
+    if (!log) {
+        return;
+    }
+    constexpr u64 step = u64{64} << 20;
+    const u64 waiting = pending_destroy.Bytes();
+    // The texture cache's figure is only read where the release below may run: both caches are
+    // locked there. Elsewhere it counts as nothing.
+    u64 images = 0;
+    if constexpr (requires { runtime.PendingImageBytes(); }) {
+        if (may_wait_for_memory) {
+            images = runtime.PendingImageBytes();
+        }
+    }
+    if (waiting >= pending_logged_bytes + step || buffer_bytes >= live_logged_bytes + step ||
+        images >= images_logged_bytes + step) {
+        pending_logged_bytes = (std::max)(pending_logged_bytes, waiting);
+        live_logged_bytes = (std::max)(live_logged_bytes, buffer_bytes);
+        images_logged_bytes = (std::max)(images_logged_bytes, images);
+        std::fprintf(stderr,
+                     "EDEN_BC_PENDING frame=%llu waiting=%llu MiB in %llu deleted buffers, the "
+                     "cache holds %llu MiB, deleted images waiting %llu MiB\n",
+                     static_cast<unsigned long long>(frame_tick),
+                     static_cast<unsigned long long>(waiting >> 20),
+                     static_cast<unsigned long long>(pending_destroy.Buffers()),
+                     static_cast<unsigned long long>(buffer_bytes >> 20),
+                     static_cast<unsigned long long>(images >> 20));
+    }
+    if (!may_wait_for_memory ||
+        !VideoCommon::PendingReleaseDue(waiting, limit, images, image_limit)) {
+        return;
+    }
+    if constexpr (requires { runtime.ReleaseForBuffer(); }) {
+        const u64 buffers = pending_destroy.Buffers();
+        // Ends in ReleaseFinished above, which empties the ring and the count, and in the texture
+        // cache's, which destroys the images the GPU is past: after the wait, all of them.
+        runtime.ReleaseForBuffer();
+        u64 images_left = 0;
+        if constexpr (requires { runtime.PendingImageBytes(); }) {
+            images_left = runtime.PendingImageBytes();
+        }
+        const u64 images_freed = images - (std::min)(images, images_left);
+        pending_released_bytes += waiting + images_freed;
+        // The 1st, 2nd, 4th, 8th ... release in the log.
+        if (const u64 times = ++pending_releases; (times & (times - 1)) == 0) {
+            std::fprintf(stderr,
+                         "EDEN_BC_PENDING release %llu at frame %llu: %llu MiB in %llu buffers and "
+                         "%llu MiB of images destroyed after a wait for the GPU (%llu MiB so far), "
+                         "still waiting: %llu MiB of buffers, %llu MiB of images\n",
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(times),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(frame_tick),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(waiting >> 20),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(buffers),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(images_freed >> 20),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(pending_released_bytes >> 20),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(pending_destroy.Bytes() >> 20),
+                         static_cast<unsigned long long>(images_left >> 20));
+        }
+    }
 }
 
